{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of S2 at head 85fd9713a0174c26b066880eb4f2f74bb0c993c2, tree 181fd7d3, for request 69080f12 and review request ce1f74e5. Verdict: APPROVED for source readiness.\n\nThe head changes five paths from main: the note, its manifest and three test paths. It changes no production file. Ruling f152f847 decides how the plan's basic-host witness counts, and this approval stays within it. The render against an S1 room stays owed, along with real-room actor and write observations.\n\nI read the note first, then the three test diffs, the patched-host record and the browser result.\n\n## Against the plan and ruling f152f847\n\n1. dap's policy is unchanged. A client without the UI capability gets text without UI metadata. The head adds a test assertion for that and changes no source.\n2. The unmodified negotiation stays as its own evidence, in receipt 3e94275d. The note reports the delta, patch SHA 27189d5e and upstream commit 82221c0c. The patched host stays in scratch, outside the checkout.\n3. The rendered witness ran on a pinned headless browser from scratch. `browser-v5/result.json` reports `passed: true` with 18 cases, no console errors and no network failures.\n4. The note names what it rendered against: a scripted fixture with synthetic custody, not a room.\n\nThe plan's witnesses:\n\n- App-only tool: `view-resources.test.ts` now asserts `visibility: [\"app\"]` for a client with the UI capability, absence from the listing without it, and a direct call that works in both. The comment says plainly that visibility describes presentation and grants nothing. It tests the metadata and listing, not what a host shows a model.\n- Agent chip: the new `view-sessions.test.ts` case pairs an agent with a controller with an agent without one. The second card is unavailable, its act is refused with `shape`, and nothing is performed.\n- Altered bytes: the existing case at `view-resources.test.ts:37` refuses them.\n- Stale head: the note leaves this with existing owners, and I did not rerun them.\n\n## What I checked in the render\n\nThe builder reviewed some images by eye and said so. I opened two that it did not name, `render-change-dark-390.png` and `render-decision-light-1280.png`. Both show the card inside the real host at the right width and theme, with \"Builder · controlled by Rita · agent\", and with no overflow.\n\nAll four resources show the same scripted card, so the Decision view shows \"work q8\". The note says so, and this proves the kit's plumbing and not S4's journey views.\n\n## The gate\n\n- The gate at bcd6615a, tree b3055250, passes all five stages. The receipt exits 0 with complete capture and the same head and tree before and after. Node passes 84 cases, Counting 56, Plain 3,193 with one skip and Native 879 with two skips.\n- From bcd6615a to the head, only the note and the manifest change, which the documents-only rule in `docs/testing.md` covers.\n- The failed attempts stay recorded as failures: browser runs V2, V3 and V4, and the first build.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 0f0a949e gives the head tree 181fd7d3.\n- The five artifacts match the five changed paths.\n- I ran `view-resources` and `view-sessions` once: 5 of 5. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 of 10. The worktree stayed clean.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 1e88087b, and all 206 rows that it holds match by SHA-256, including the note. Each unit's `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is writable:\n  - browser: 302 files, 22,379,034 bytes, digest 9b7897bc;\n  - gate: 253 files, 60,502,943 bytes, digest e272f667;\n  - focused: 122 files, 16,465,681 bytes, digest 6e6fc4cd.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 774 links, 0 broken. check-notes from main: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages: 6 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The inventory says that basic-host acceptance \"must demonstrate the required host-neutral path\", because `resources.ts` calls `sandboxDomain` unconditionally. No later section closes that sentence. The witness ran with that call in place, so the note should say so.\n2. `fixture` is newly exported from `views-host.ts`, and only the scratch browser packet uses it. The repeatable browser witness therefore lives in the evidence unit, not in the gate. The ruling allows that, and it means a later change to these views gets no automatic render check against basic-host.\n3. The note still uses \"Root\" for the builder, and its inventory table describes an older base, which it says.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe kit stays in its existing owners, the head adds no kernel part, and host-specific code stays in `views/hosts.ts`. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nViews hold no keys. The service signs from server-side custody, and the browser witness counts one signature for the accepted action and one for the lost reply, with no second original sent. The exact-Origin adapter belongs to the fixture and says that it proves no production Origin policy. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe head adds two assertions and one case, and it reuses a fixture. It adds no production code. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the kit's source, the corrected-host witness, the gate and the evidence hold. Unmodified-host compatibility, S1-room rendering, real-room actors and writes, hosted behaviour and S4's views are not shown, and the note claims none of them.\n- No deployment follows from this head, because it changes no production file.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f2bbb675880e436094ed9589883b4df6e52ba4c4","binding":"assigned","head":"85fd9713a0174c26b066880eb4f2f74bb0c993c2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da9018a474a39fb3e10042aa536c06fec26694b3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:46b4a8fbe5a0d1b48ee1c18179dd51f56e8923d3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da9018a474a39fb3e10042aa536c06fec26694b3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}